  "difficulty_level": "H2",
  "difficulty_reason": "The counted proof does not evaluate any single semigroup example: it must produce, in each parity case, a four-generator family whose Kunz nilsemigroup has a prescribed poset, prove that every Apery element has a unique factorization by separating residue classes modulo m, and then eliminate every candidate outer Betti element through an explicit chained inequality. The realization mechanism is uniform in k and m under the exact quadratic hypothesis 4m>=(eta-2)^2, and the final count eta(S)=2k+4 or 2k+3 comes from the Kunz poset rather than from an exhibited minimal presentation. This is research-level construction and verification of a genuinely new family, not a routine corollary of the retained local core, and it stays above ordinary PhD qualifying algebra.",
